<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "12564"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "“To the Leadenhall Street Post Office, to be left till called for." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "12977"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "12631"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "He said that if they were sent to the office he would be chaffed by all the other clerks about having letters from a lady, so I offered to typewrite them, like he did his, but he wouldn’t have that, for he said that when I wrote them they seemed to come from me, but when they were typewritten he always felt that the machine had come between us." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13083"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "12978"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "That will just show you how fond he was of me, Mr. Holmes, and the little things that he would think of.”" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049.S03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inSection> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/section/III> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#order> "49"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#printedPage> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#revealedBy> "C1" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#speaker> <http://example.org/dectective/story/mary> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P049> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Paragraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13123"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13085"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "“It was most suggestive,” said Holmes." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13216"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13124"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "“It has long been an axiom of mine that the little things are infinitely the most important." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13282"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13217"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Can you remember any other little things about Mr. Hosmer Angel?”" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050.S03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inSection> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/section/III> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#order> "50"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#printedPage> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#revealedBy> "C1" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#speaker> <http://example.org/dectective/story/holmes> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P050> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Paragraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13319"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13284"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "“He was a very shy man, Mr. Holmes." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13430"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13320"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "He would rather walk with me in the evening than in the daylight, for he said that he hated to be conspicuous." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13468"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13431"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Very retiring and gentlemanly he was." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13495"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13469"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Even his voice was gentle." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13653"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13496"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "He’d had the quinsy and swollen glands when he was young, he told me, and it had left him with a weak throat, and a hesitating, whispering fashion of speech." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S05> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S06> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13791"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S06> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S06> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13654"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S06> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "He was always well dressed, very neat and plain, but his eyes were weak, just as mine are, and he wore tinted glasses against the glare.”" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051.S06> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inSection> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/section/III> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#order> "51"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#printedPage> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#revealedBy> "C1" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#speaker> <http://example.org/dectective/story/mary> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P051> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Paragraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13875"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13793"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "“Well, and what happened when Mr. Windibank, your stepfather, returned to France?”" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052.S01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inSection> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/section/III> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#order> "52"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#printedPage> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#revealedBy> "C1" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#speaker> <http://example.org/dectective/story/holmes> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P052> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Paragraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "13977"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13877"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "“Mr. Hosmer Angel came to the house again and proposed that we should marry before father came back." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "14109"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "13978"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "He was in dreadful earnest and made me swear, with my hands on the Testament, that whatever happened I would always be true to him." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "14197"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "14110"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Mother said he was quite right to make me swear, and that it was a sign of his passion." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "14280"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "14198"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Mother was all in his favour from the first and was even fonder of him than I was." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "14495"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "14281"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Then, when they talked of marrying within the week, I began to ask about father; but they both said never to mind about father, but just to tell him afterwards, and mother said she would make it all right with him." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S05> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S06> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "14533"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S06> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S06> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "14496"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S06> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "I didn’t quite like that, Mr. Holmes." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S06> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S07> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "14809"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S07> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S07> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "14534"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S07> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "It seemed funny that I should ask his leave, as he was only a few years older than me; but I didn’t want to do anything on the sly, so I wrote to father at Bordeaux, where the company has its French offices, but the letter came back to me on the very morning of the wedding.”" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053.S07> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P053> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inSection> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/section/III> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
