<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P089.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "One was buttoned only in the two lower buttons out of five, and the other at the first, third, and fifth." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P089.S03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P089.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "22351"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P089.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P089> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P089.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "22170"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P089.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Now, when you see that a young lady, otherwise neatly dressed, has come away from home with odd boots, half-buttoned, it is no great deduction to say that she came away in a hurry.”" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P089.S04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
