<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P100> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Paragraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "25178"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "24897"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "I had had so many reasons to believe in my friend’s subtle powers of reasoning and extraordinary energy in action that I felt that he must have some solid grounds for the assured and easy demeanour with which he treated the singular mystery which he had been called upon to fathom." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "25498"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "25179"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Once only had I known him to fail, in the case of the King of Bohemia and of the Irene Adler photograph; but when I looked back to the weird business of the Sign of Four, and the extraordinary circumstances connected with the Study in Scarlet, I felt that it would be a strange tangle indeed which he could not unravel." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101.S02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inSection> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/section/IV> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#order> "101"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#printedPage> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
