<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P101> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Paragraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "25762"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "25500"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "I left him then, still puffing at his black clay pipe, with the conviction that when I came again on the next evening I would find that he held in his hands all the clues which would lead up to the identity of the disappearing bridegroom of Miss Mary Sutherland." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102.S01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inSection> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/section/IV> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#order> "102"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#printedPage> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#revealedBy> "C3" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#speaker> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#narrator> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P102> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Paragraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "25912"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "25764"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "A professional case of great gravity was engaging my own attention at the time, and the whole of next day I was busy at the bedside of the sufferer." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "26129"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "25913"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "It was not until close upon six o’clock that I found myself free and was able to spring into a hansom and drive to Baker Street, half afraid that I might be too late to assist at the dénouement of the little mystery." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "26250"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "26130"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "I found Sherlock Holmes alone, however, half asleep, with his long, thin form curled up in the recesses of his armchair." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "26430"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "26251"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "A formidable array of bottles and test-tubes, with the pungent cleanly smell of hydrochloric acid, told me that he had spent his day in the chemical work which was so dear to him." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103.S04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inSection> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/section/V> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#order> "103"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P103> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#printedPage> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
