<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P115> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#speaker> <http://example.org/dectective/story/windibank> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P115> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Paragraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "28731"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "28608"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S01> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "“It is a curious thing,” remarked Holmes, “that a typewriter has really quite as much individuality as a man’s handwriting." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "28794"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "28732"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S02> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Unless they are quite new, no two of them write exactly alike." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "28866"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "28795"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S03> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Some letters get more worn than others, and some wear only on one side." <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "29030"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "28867"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S04> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "Now, you remark in this note of yours, Mr. Windibank, that in every case there is some little slurring over of the ‘e,’ and a slight defect in the tail of the ‘r.’" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#endOffset> "29105"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#inParagraph> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#startOffset> "29031"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S05> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#text> "There are fourteen other characteristics, but those are the more obvious.”" <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
<http://example.org/dectective/edition/text/P116.S05> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/dectective/edition#Sentence> <http://example.org/dectective/edition/text> .
